<Doc lang={lang} page="blocks" current="Combination" title="Combination"
  description="The Combination blocks of FLOAT (S-H-O, H-O, RGB, LRGB): one stack per filter of a monochrome camera combined into one colour image, with the steps of a recipe and the published sources.">

  <p class="kicker">Block</p>
  <h1>Combination</h1>
  <p class="meta">FLOAT 0.2.0 · beta of {release.date.en}</p>

  <dl class="inshort"><div><dt>What it does</dt><dd>It makes one colour image from the stacks of several filters of a monochrome camera, or from the channels of a dual-band image.</dd></div><div><dt>What it shows</dt><dd>One colour image, which goes on through the chain as any stack does, with the scale of each channel given in the log.</dd></div><div><dt>What can be set</dt><dd>For S-H-O and H-O, the hue of each filter; the defaults suit most images, and Channel weights sets the share of each filter.</dd></div></dl>

